{
  "concept": "A shallow neural network is a single input fed through D hidden units — each hidden unit applies its own weighted-plus-bias linear function (θ) before a ReLU, and the output is a weighted-plus-bias combination (φ) of those hidden activations.",
  "figureType": "network_diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Panel label 'a)' on the left half and 'b)' on the right half",
    "Panel a: input node circle labeled x (black outline, left)",
    "Panel a: three hidden node circles labeled h_1, h_2, h_3 (black outline, middle column, vertically stacked)",
    "Panel a: small teal ReLU 'kink' glyph drawn inside each hidden node circle",
    "Panel a: output node circle labeled y (black outline, right)",
    "Panel a: orange bias node circle labeled 1 feeding the hidden layer (upper-left, orange outline and orange text)",
    "Panel a: orange bias node circle labeled 1 feeding the output (top-center, orange outline)",
    "Panel a: black arrows x -> h_1, x -> h_2, x -> h_3 (input-to-hidden connections)",
    "Panel a: orange arrows bias1 -> h_1, bias1 -> h_2, bias1 -> h_3",
    "Panel a: orange arrow output-bias -> y",
    "Panel a: black arrows h_1 -> y, h_2 -> y, h_3 -> y (hidden-to-output connections)",
    "Panel a: orange weight labels θ_10, θ_20, θ_30 on the bias-to-hidden arrows",
    "Panel a: grey weight labels θ_11, θ_21, θ_31 on the x-to-hidden arrows",
    "Panel a: orange weight label φ_0 on the output-bias arrow",
    "Panel a: grey weight labels φ_1, φ_2, φ_3 on the hidden-to-output arrows",
    "Panel b: identical node layout (x, h_1, h_2, h_3, y) with all-black arrows, no bias nodes, no weight labels",
    "Arrowheads converging at y drawn as multiple overlapping black arrowheads",
    "Optional equation annotation beneath panel a: h_i = a[θ_i0 + θ_i1 x], y = φ_0 + Σ φ_i h_i"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "labelView",
      "type": "toggle",
      "label": "Diagram view",
      "options": ["Clean (panel b)", "Fully labeled (panel a)"],
      "default": "Clean (panel b)",
      "teaches": "The same network topology carries hidden parameters: the bare arrow diagram and the θ/φ-annotated diagram describe identical computation, one just names every parameter."
    },
    {
      "id": "selectHidden",
      "type": "click",
      "teaches": "Each hidden unit owns exactly one slope θ_i1, one bias θ_i0, and one output weight φ_i — clicking traces that single unit's private path from x through the ReLU to y."
    },
    {
      "id": "hiddenCount",
      "type": "slider",
      "label": "Number of hidden units D",
      "range": [1, 6, 1],
      "default": 3,
      "teaches": "The network's capacity is set by D: adding a hidden unit adds two θ parameters and one φ parameter, while x and y stay single nodes."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The bare network",
      "narration": "One input x fans out to three hidden units, which all feed a single output y. This is the entire architecture of a shallow network — no parameters shown yet.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Clean (panel b)", "hiddenCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Name every parameter",
      "narration": "Switching to the labeled view adds the two orange bias nodes and every weight name: θ_i0 and θ_i1 on the input side, φ_0 and φ_i on the output side.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Fully labeled (panel a)", "hiddenCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Follow one hidden unit",
      "narration": "Click h_2: its incoming pair θ_20 (bias) and θ_21 (slope from x) form the pre-activation, the teal kink applies the ReLU, and φ_2 scales its contribution to y.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Fully labeled (panel a)", "hiddenCount": 3 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Grow the hidden layer",
      "narration": "Drag D up to six. Each new unit brings its own θ_i0, θ_i1 and φ_i, so the parameter count grows as 3D + 1 while the input and output remain single nodes.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Fully labeled (panel a)", "hiddenCount": 6 }
    },
    {
      "title": "Shrink to one unit",
      "narration": "With D = 1 the network collapses to a single kinked line: y = φ_0 + φ_1·a[θ_10 + θ_11 x]. Everything richer is just a sum of more such pieces.",
      "state": { "labelView": "Fully labeled (panel a)", "hiddenCount": 1 }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "A shallow network is nothing more than D independent copies of 'scale-and-shift x, clip it, then scale again' — the θ's build each hidden unit's kinked line and the φ's decide how much of each line to add into the output.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Two side-by-side panels sharing an identical left-to-right node layout: input circle x on the left, a vertical column of hidden circles h_1..h_D in the middle, output circle y on the right, all white with black outlines and italic serif labels. Panel b (right) is the clean version: plain black arrows only, arrowheads piling up at y. Panel a (left) adds two salmon/orange bias circles labeled '1' — one up-left feeding every hidden unit, one at top-center feeding y — drawn in orange outline with orange arrows, while x-to-hidden and hidden-to-output arrows stay black. Weight labels sit just above each arrow: orange labels for bias weights (θ_10, θ_20, θ_30, φ_0), grey labels for signal weights (θ_11, θ_21, θ_31, φ_1, φ_2, φ_3). Inside each hidden circle draw a small teal ReLU kink glyph (flat segment joining a rising segment). When a hidden unit is clicked, bolden and saturate its three connected arrows and their labels while fading all other edges to light grey. The hidden-unit slider should re-space the column symmetrically about the x–y axis and renumber labels; bias arrows must re-fan to the new unit positions. Generous white background, no axes, no legend."
}

